For a baseline understanding of what's happening in vulnerable environments, here's what's driving those error conditions. Error-based injection occurs when a database statement runs without checking whether the input supports the operation — because the input is sanitized, the query will match SELECT * from tablestructures against tables that are actively filtered by the query to return them. That's why even benign queries trigger the payload: they just strip away controls.

